    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493295765/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """which he thinks is not genuine. He said she ought to consider it such a privilege to go with a man of such vast knowledge and experience as he had, that she ought to accept everything he said!
Bernhard is reading  Karl Pearson’s Grammar of Science , and finds it a splendid piece of clear thinking, and the most destructive to Catholicism that there has yet been. I must remember this for Ray and Karin.
A letter from Miss Sellers says: “Let us all get very rich, and hire a yacht and go to places. I will not say where the vulgar have not penetrated, for they penetrate everywhere, but only when the vulgar are not there.” """^^xsd:string ;
